## Environment variables

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill in any values marked as required:

```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

All `.env` reads in this project go through `{{ pkg_name }}.env.get_env()`,
which caches the parsed file so the disk is only read once per process.  To
force a re-read (e.g. in tests that write to `.env`):

```python
from {{ pkg_name }}.env import reload_env
reload_env()
```
